2. BUILD A LEAK-FREE HISTORICAL CLEAN SHEET DATASET
==================================================

Create a historical per-fixture dataset.

One row must represent:

(season, gameweek, fixture_id, team_id)

This is a TEAM-FIXTURE clean-sheet prediction problem.

Target:

clean_sheet = 1 if team conceded 0 goals
clean_sheet = 0 otherwise

Features must contain ONLY information available before the fixture.

Potential features:

TEAM DEFENSIVE STRENGTH
- goals conceded per 90
- shots conceded
- shots on target conceded
- xGA if available
- clean sheets in recent matches
- home/away defensive performance
- recent defensive form
- opponent-adjusted defensive strength

OPPONENT ATTACK
- goals scored per 90
- shots
- shots on target
- xG if available
- recent attacking form
- home/away attacking performance

FIXTURE
- home/away
- opponent defensive strength where relevant
- opponent attacking strength
- fixture difficulty
- team strength ratings

MINUTES / PLAYER AVAILABILITY
Do not make clean-sheet probability dependent on one specific defender.

This is primarily a TEAM-level prediction.

No future match statistics.

No post-match data.

No leakage.

==================================================
3. TRAIN CLEAN SHEET MODELS
==================================================

Build at least:

Baseline:
existing deterministic/statistical clean-sheet model.

ML candidate:
a suitable probabilistic classifier such as LightGBM/XGBoost/logistic regression depending on dataset size and existing infrastructure.

The model should output:

P(clean sheet)

Evaluate using strict chronological out-of-sample testing.

Use:

- LogLoss
- Brier score
- calibration
- ROC-AUC as secondary metric
- MAE if useful

Calibration is especially important.

A model predicting:

0.70

should approximately produce clean sheets 70% of the time in comparable out-of-sample cases.

Do NOT deploy the ML model merely because its raw accuracy is higher.

It must produce better calibrated probabilities and demonstrate improvement over the baseline.

