12. FPL SCORING ENGINE
==================================================

Keep the scoring engine deterministic.

ML models predict probabilities/rates.

The scoring engine converts them into expected FPL points.

For example:

Expected CS points =
P(clean sheet) × position-specific CS points × probability player plays enough minutes

Expected DEFCON points =
P(DEFCON) × 2

subject to the correct FPL rules.

Do not double-count minutes.

Do not double-count clean sheets.

Do not double-count DEFCON.

Document the exact expected-value equations.

